    <!-- Common Mistakes Section -->
    <section style="margin: 2.5rem 0;" aria-labelledby="mistakes-heading">
      <h2 id="mistakes-heading">Common Mistakes When Measuring Date Spans</h2>
      <ul style="color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.8; margin-left: 1.25rem;">
        <li><strong>Forgetting the Fencepost (Inclusive) Error:</strong> If you stay at a hotel from Friday to Sunday, you stayed 2 nights (exclusive), but were present across 3 calendar days (inclusive). Be sure to toggle the inclusive checkbox depending on whether you are calculating night duration or day coverage.</li>
        <li><strong>Treating Business Days as 5/7 of Total Days:</strong> While the ratio is roughly 5/7 (~71.4%), the exact count of working days depends heavily on which day of the week the span starts and ends on. Our algorithm iterates every calendar date to accurately tally Monday through Friday.</li>
        <li><strong>Public Holidays:</strong> This calculator computes standard Monday–Friday business days. It does not automatically exclude bank or public holidays because statutory holidays vary by country, state, and company.</li>
      </ul>
